* kindling proof model
*
* 2 variables, 2 constraints
*
* --- x1 in [0, 1], the model's a ---
* x1 = 1*x1b0
*
* x1ge{v} means x1 >= v.  veripb accepts reification
* arrows in proof files but not in .opb files, so the two constraints
* per value below are the big-M spelling of what we would rather write:
*     x1ge{v} ==> 1*x1b0 >= v      (_up)
*     x1ge{v} <== 1*x1b0 >= v      (_dn)
@x1ge1_up 1 x1b0 1 ~x1ge1 >= 1 ;
@x1ge1_dn 1 ~x1b0 1 x1ge1 >= 1 ;
* x1eq{v} means x1 = v, which is x1ge{v} and not x1ge{v+1}
@x1eq0_up0 1 ~x1eq0 1 ~x1ge1 >= 1 ;
@x1eq0_dn 1 x1eq0 1 x1ge1 >= 1 ;
@x1eq1_up0 1 ~x1eq1 1 x1ge1 >= 1 ;
@x1eq1_dn 1 x1eq1 1 ~x1ge1 >= 1 ;
*
* --- x2 in [0, 1], the model's b ---
* x2 = 1*x2b0
*
* x2ge{v} means x2 >= v.  veripb accepts reification
* arrows in proof files but not in .opb files, so the two constraints
* per value below are the big-M spelling of what we would rather write:
*     x2ge{v} ==> 1*x2b0 >= v      (_up)
*     x2ge{v} <== 1*x2b0 >= v      (_dn)
@x2ge1_up 1 x2b0 1 ~x2ge1 >= 1 ;
@x2ge1_dn 1 ~x2b0 1 x2ge1 >= 1 ;
* x2eq{v} means x2 = v, which is x2ge{v} and not x2ge{v+1}
@x2eq0_up0 1 ~x2eq0 1 ~x2ge1 >= 1 ;
@x2eq0_dn 1 x2eq0 1 x2ge1 >= 1 ;
@x2eq1_up0 1 ~x2eq1 1 x2ge1 >= 1 ;
@x2eq1_dn 1 x2eq1 1 ~x2ge1 >= 1 ;
*
* table(x1, x2) with 2 tuples
@tbl1_sel 1 c1t0 1 c1t1 >= 1 ;
@tbl1t0_1 1 ~c1t0 1 x1eq0 >= 1 ;
@tbl1t0_2 1 ~c1t0 1 x2eq0 >= 1 ;
@tbl1t1_1 1 ~c1t1 1 x1eq1 >= 1 ;
@tbl1t1_2 1 ~c1t1 1 x2eq1 >= 1 ;
*
* table(x1, x2) with 2 tuples
@tbl2_sel 1 c2t0 1 c2t1 >= 1 ;
@tbl2t0_1 1 ~c2t0 1 x1eq0 >= 1 ;
@tbl2t0_2 1 ~c2t0 1 x2eq1 >= 1 ;
@tbl2t1_1 1 ~c2t1 1 x1eq1 >= 1 ;
@tbl2t1_2 1 ~c2t1 1 x2eq0 >= 1 ;
